      "text": "The first term, when $n = 0,$ is $1/x.$  The next term is\n\\[\\frac{1}{x^x - x^{-x}}.\\]The next term is\n\\[\\frac{1}{x^{x^x} - x^{-x^x}}.\\]Doing one more step, we get\n\\[\\frac{1}{x^{x^{x^x}} - x^{-x^{x^x}}}.\\]In general, when $n > 0,$ the $n$th term is\n\\[\\frac{1}{x^{x^{x^{\\hdots^{x}}}} - x^{-x^{x^{\\hdots^{x}}}}}.\\]To close this telescoping sum, the $n$th term must cancel the $n - 1$th term, which is\n\\[\\frac{1}{x^{x^{x^{\\hdots^{x}}} - x^{-x^{x^{\\hdots^{x}}}}}}.\\]If we multiply numerator and denominator by $-1,$ this becomes\n\\[\\frac{-1}{x^{-x^{x^{\\hdots^{x}}} - x^{x^{x^{\\hdots^{x}}}}}.\\]Now we can write the sum as\n\\[\\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{-1}{x^{x - 1}}/x + \\frac{-1}{x^{x^2 - x}}/x^2 + \\frac{-1}{x^{x^3 - x^2}}/x^3 + \\dotso.\\]Thus, the infinite series telescopes to\n\\[\\boxed{\\frac{x}{x - 1}}.\\]. The answer is \\frac{x}{x-1}",
